A good smell of spices comes from the kitchen.
The curry is boiling on the stove.
Then I hear a sound at the door.
I open the door.
Kiran and Sara are standing at the door.
They have wet umbrellas in their hands.
First, they close the umbrellas.
"Leave the umbrellas there," I say.
They shake the water off the umbrellas.
After that, "Maya, what a good smell!" Sara says happily.
"It is the smell of chicken curry," Kiran says.
"Yes, I am making chicken curry," I say.
The curry needs five more minutes to be ready.
Then, I invite them inside.
